// ============================================================================
// The mark, the wordmark, and the lockup they make together.
//
// One rule governs this file: the phone draws the SAME artwork as everything
// else, not a phone-shaped impression of it. Every number below was measured
// off the master lockup, "Where your story falls into place..svg", by pulling
// the two flat images out of it and counting pixels. Nothing here is a guess
// and nothing here is a taste call.
//
//   The mark      is the SVG in `MARK` in public/app.js, coordinate for
//                 coordinate. Its viewBox is "14 8 36 50.5" and its bottom
//                 edge is the type baseline.
//
//   The wordmark  is beatfall-brand/wordmark/beatfall-wordmark.svg from the
//                 brand pack: Newsreader SemiBold outlined to paths at
//                 font-size 200 (upem 2000, so one font unit is 0.1 here).
//                 Outlines, not live text, so the letterforms cannot drift
//                 with a font that failed to load or a platform that fakes
//                 the weight. "Beat" is ink, "fall" is blue. That split IS
//                 the wordmark; a one-colour "beatfall" is a different mark.
//
// Both are drawn inside ONE <Svg>, in one coordinate space where the wordmark
// em is 200 units. That is deliberate: two sibling views cannot be aligned on
// a baseline in React Native, and every attempt to fake it with margins came
// out crooked at one size or another.
//
// If either drawing changes on the web, change it here. There is no build
// step that keeps them in step, only this comment and the fact that they are
// literally the same numbers.
// ============================================================================
